<section id="iii" class="ltx_subsection">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">§23.10(iii) </span><math class="ltx_Math" altimg="m45.png" altimg-height="13px" altimg-valign="-2px" altimg-width="17px" alttext="n" display="inline"><mi href="./23.1#t1.r2" title="integer">n</mi></math>-Tuple Formulas</h2>
<div id="iii.info" class="ltx_metadata ltx_info">
<span href="" class="ltx_infoicon ltx_icon" title="Show Annotations"><span class="ltx_font_bold">ⓘ</span></span>
<div class="ltx_infocontent">
<dl>
<dt>Keywords:</dt>
<dd>
<a class="ltx_keyword" href="./search/search?q=Weierstrass%20elliptic%20functions">Weierstrass elliptic functions</a>, <a class="ltx_keyword" href="./search/search?q=n-tuple%20formulas"><math class="ltx_Math" altimg="m45.png" altimg-height="13px" altimg-valign="-2px" altimg-width="17px" alttext="n" display="inline"><mi href="./23.1#t1.r2" title="integer">n</mi></math>-tuple formulas</a>
</dd>
<dt>Notes:</dt>
<dd>See <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet">Lawden (<a href="./bib/L#bib1385" title="Elliptic Functions and Applications" class="ltx_ref">1989</a>, §6.6)</cite>.
For (<a href="./23.10#E11" title="(23.10.11) ‣ §23.10(iii) 𝑛-Tuple Formulas ‣ §23.10 Addition Theorems and Other Identities ‣ Weierstrass Elliptic Functions ‣ Chapter 23 Weierstrass Elliptic and Modular Functions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">23.10.11</span></a>) and (<a href="./23.10#E12" title="(23.10.12) ‣ §23.10(iii) 𝑛-Tuple Formulas ‣ §23.10 Addition Theorems and Other Identities ‣ Weierstrass Elliptic Functions ‣ Chapter 23 Weierstrass Elliptic and Modular Functions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">23.10.12</span></a>)
compare the poles and residues of the two sides.
(<a href="./23.10#E13" title="(23.10.13) ‣ §23.10(iii) 𝑛-Tuple Formulas ‣ §23.10 Addition Theorems and Other Identities ‣ Weierstrass Elliptic Functions ‣ Chapter 23 Weierstrass Elliptic and Modular Functions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">23.10.13</span></a>) follows by integration.
For (<a href="./23.10#E15" title="(23.10.15) ‣ §23.10(iii) 𝑛-Tuple Formulas ‣ §23.10 Addition Theorems and Other Identities ‣ Weierstrass Elliptic Functions ‣ Chapter 23 Weierstrass Elliptic and Modular Functions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">23.10.15</span></a>) combine (<a href="./23.10#E14" title="(23.10.14) ‣ §23.10(iii) 𝑛-Tuple Formulas ‣ §23.10 Addition Theorems and Other Identities ‣ Weierstrass Elliptic Functions ‣ Chapter 23 Weierstrass Elliptic and Modular Functions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">23.10.14</span></a>),
(<a href="./23.8#E7" title="(23.8.7) ‣ §23.8(iii) Infinite Products ‣ §23.8 Trigonometric Series and Products ‣ Weierstrass Elliptic Functions ‣ Chapter 23 Weierstrass Elliptic and Modular Functions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">23.8.7</span></a>), and (<a href="./4.21#E35" title="(4.21.35) ‣ De Moivre’s Theorem ‣ §4.21(iii) Multiples of the Argument ‣ §4.21 Identities ‣ Trigonometric Functions ‣ Chapter 4 Elementary Functions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.21.35</span></a>).</dd>
<dt>Permalink:</dt>
<dd><a href="./23.10.iii" title="" class="ltx_ref">http://dlmf.nist.gov/23.10.iii</a></dd>
<dt>See also:</dt>
<dd>Annotations for <a href="./23.10#info" title="§23.10 Addition Theorems and Other Identities ‣ Weierstrass Elliptic Functions ‣ Chapter 23 Weierstrass Elliptic and Modular Functions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">§23.10</span></a> and
<a href="./23#info" title="Chapter 23 Weierstrass Elliptic and Modular Functions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Ch.23</span></a>
</dd>
</dl>
</div>
</div>

<div id="iii.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p class="ltx_p">For <math class="ltx_Math" altimg="m44.png" altimg-height="21px" altimg-valign="-6px" altimg-width="108px" alttext="n=2,3,\dots" display="inline"><mrow><mi href="./23.1#t1.r2" title="integer">n</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow></mrow></math>,</p>
<div class="ltx_equation_container">
<table id="E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody>
<tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">23.10.11</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math class="ltx_Math" altimg="E11.png" altimg-height="113px" altimg-valign="-31px" altimg-width="393px" alttext="n^{2}\wp\left(nz\right)=\sum_{j=0}^{n-1}\sum_{\ell=0}^{n-1}\wp\left(z+\frac{2j%
}{n}\omega_{1}+\frac{2\ell}{n}\omega_{3}\right)," display="block"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi href="./23.1#t1.r2" title="integer">n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>⁢</mo><mrow><mi href="./23.2#E4" mathvariant="normal" title="Weierstrass ℘-function">℘</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi href="./23.1#t1.r2" title="integer">n</mi><mo>⁢</mo><mi href="./23.1#t1.r4" title="complex">z</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi href="./23.1#t1.r2" title="integer">n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi href="./23.1#t1.r2" title="integer">n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><mi href="./23.2#E4" mathvariant="normal" title="Weierstrass ℘-function">℘</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi href="./23.1#t1.r4" title="complex">z</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>⁢</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi href="./23.1#t1.r2" title="integer">n</mi></mfrac><mo>⁢</mo><msub><mi href="./23.1#t1.r8" title="lattice generators">ω</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>⁢</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mi href="./23.1#t1.r2" title="integer">n</mi></mfrac><mo>⁢</mo><msub><mi href="./23.1#t1.r8" title="lattice generators">ω</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr>
<tr><td class="ltx_align_right" colspan="4">
<div id="E11.info" class="ltx_metadata ltx_info">
<span href="" class="ltx_infoicon ltx_icon" title="Show Annotations"><span class="ltx_font_bold">ⓘ</span></span>
<div class="ltx_infocontent">
<dl>
<dt>Symbols:</dt>
<dd>
<a href="./23.2#E4" title="(23.2.4) ‣ §23.2(ii) Weierstrass Elliptic Functions ‣ §23.2 Definitions and Periodic Properties ‣ Weierstrass Elliptic Functions ‣ Chapter 23 Weierstrass Elliptic and Modular Functions" class="ltx_ref"><math class="ltx_Math" altimg="m28.png" altimg-height="25px" altimg-valign="-7px" altimg-width="48px" alttext="\wp\left(\NVar{z}\right)" display="inline"><mrow><mi href="./23.2#E4" mathvariant="normal" title="Weierstrass ℘-function">℘</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi class="ltx_nvar" href="./23.1#t1.r4" title="complex">z</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></math>
(= <math class="ltx_Math" altimg="m30.png" altimg-height="25px" altimg-valign="-7px" altimg-width="67px" alttext="\wp\left(z|\mathbb{L}\right)" display="inline"><mrow><mi href="./23.2#E4" mathvariant="normal" title="Weierstrass ℘-function">℘</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi href="./23.1#t1.r4" title="complex">z</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi href="./23.1#t1.r1" title="lattice">𝕃</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></math> = <math class="ltx_Math" altimg="m29.png" altimg-height="25px" altimg-valign="-7px" altimg-width="105px" alttext="\wp\left(z;g_{2},g_{3}\right)" display="inline"><mrow><mi href="./23.3#E8" mathvariant="normal" title="Weierstrass ℘-function">℘</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi href="./23.1#t1.r4" title="complex">z</mi><mo>;</mo><mrow><msub><mi href="./23.3#EGx1" title="Weierstrass lattice invariants 𝑔₂⁡, 𝑔₃⁡">g</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi href="./23.3#EGx1" title="Weierstrass lattice invariants 𝑔₂⁡, 𝑔₃⁡">g</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></math>): Weierstrass <math class="ltx_Math" altimg="m27.png" altimg-height="17px" altimg-valign="-6px" altimg-width="18px" alttext="\wp" display="inline"><mi href="./23.2#E4" mathvariant="normal" title="Weierstrass ℘-function">℘</mi></math>-function</a>,
